      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-2538",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the function $y = \\sqrt{\\frac{x^{2} + 1}{x + 1}}$. The derivative of this function is given by\n$y^{\u2032} = (g(x))/(2(x + 1)^{3/2}\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1})$.\n\nFind the function $g(x)$."
