      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-138848",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the function $y=\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+6x){sin}^{2}x}.$  The derivative of this function for $x\\in (0,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{'}=\\frac{g(x)\\operatorname{sin}x+h(x)\\operatorname{cos}x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+6x}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x)+h(x).$"
